SUMMARY:Canadian Premiere Anchorball After Dark\, Royal Botanical Gardens 
 (Burlington)
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\nOn **Saturday September 5th\,** **join us 
 for the Canadian Premiere of Anchorball at The Royal Botanical Gardens (RB
 G) After Dark Event in Burlington.**\nRBG After Dark transforms ANCHORBALL
 : A Curious Art Journey into a vibrant evening experience for adults. Expl
 ore the gardens after hours surrounded by 18 large-scale pop art sculpture
 s\, illuminated pathways\, live entertainment\, food\, drinks\, and intera
 ctive experiences throughout the night. We will have the pleasure of walki
 ng through these beautiful gardens (the number one spot for wedding photos
 ) and seeing the Canadian Premiere of Anchorball. This way we see the Gard
 ens in daylight\, and also lit up at night. **Purchase your ticket for RBG
  After Dark Anchorball on Saturday September 5th.**\n\nExplore the vibrant
  sculptural universe of artist and contemporary sculptor Ken Kelleher\, in
 ternationally known as Anchorball. This massive outdoor exhibition transfo
 rms the garden into a vivid sculptural landscape where bold characters\, i
 maginative narratives\, and contemporary form merge with nature and blooms
  to create a world that feels full of wonder\, yet deeply recognizable.\n\
 nFeaturing 18 monumental sculptures ranging up to 12 feet tall\, the exhib
 ition introduces visitors to an evolving fictional universe\, known as Low
  Orbit City\, populated by playful and mythical characters. In addition to
  the physical installations\, visitors can discover a hidden digital world
  using augmented reality with characters known as Cloudwalkers and unlock 
 an AR Masterpiece\, extending the experience beyond the visible landscape 
 and inviting moments of surprise\, play\, and exploration throughout the g
 arden.\n\nThere will also be an acrylic paint workshop at 7 and 8pm for 30
 mins.\n\n**WEATHER POLICY**:\n\n* This is an outdoor event and is subject 
 to weather conditions. RBG reserves the right to postpone\, reschedule\, o
 r cancel the event due to inclement weather\, unforeseen circumstances\, o
 r other conditions that may impact safety. Ticket holders will be notified
  of any changes via email\, which may occur without prior notice.\n\n**TRA
 NSPORTATION**:\n\n* Arrange for your own transportation. Feel free to post
  in the Comments if you want/need to carpool.\n* **Carpool attendees MUST 
 have a picture and arrange a PUBLIC pick-up/ drop off spot for the securit
 y of members**. Any risks associated with carpooling are borne by the memb
 er\, and Experience Toronto cannot be held liable under any circumstances.
 \n\n**COST**\nGeneral Admission: $27 + service fee + taxes\n\nMeetup Organ
 izer Fee: $10\n\nThere are no refunds.\n\n***\n\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSV
 P Yes** **with your cell and email (required for out of town events)**\; *
 *everyone goes on the waitlist until they post they have purchased their t
 icket and have transportation)**\n* **[Purchase](https://secure.rbg.ca/991
 5/11200)**[ ](https://www.tcomusic.ca/concert/opera-highlights-all-the-gre
 atest-moments/#season-passes)your own ticket for **RBG After Dark Anchorba
 ll on Saturday September 5th\, p**ost you have purchased your ticket and h
 ave transportation\, and I will move you to going.\n\nA reminder will be s
 ent the day before with my cell and details where to meet and when.\n\nRSV
 Ps close 2 days prior\, hoping there are still tickets\, and the Waitlist 
 will be removed at that time. Cancellations will result in a No Show and i
 mpact future attendance.\n\n***\n\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me at: 6:30pm a
 t Hendrie Park\, Royal Botanical Gardens at 680 Plains Rd. W. in Burlingto
 n\, to the right of the entrance before scanning your tickets. We will the
 n head in together.**\n\n**Time: 6:30 - 10:30pm** (people can leave whenev
 er they wish)\n\n**8:30pm: I have made reservations for dinner a few mins 
 away.** I hope you will join.\n\nEnjoy and please post your comments in th
 e Event after.
