SUMMARY:Bunker Drama Thriller at TIFF 2026 + Lunch (Princess of Wales)
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\n**On Tuesday September 15th\,** **see Bunk
 er at the 51st edition of the Toronto International Film Festival (TIFF)**
 . Oscar winners Penélope Cruz and Javier Bardem play a couple whose bond 
 is tested when a mysterious billionaire’s proposal prompts an ethical im
 passe in the latest from Oscar-winning writer-director Florian Zeller (TIF
 F ’20’s *The Father*). When a mysterious billionaire asks Miguel (Bard
 em) to design a luxury bunker where a tiny cluster of the ultra-wealthy ca
 n take shelter in an apocalypse\, the offer appeals to his vanity as much 
 as his pocketbook - an opportunity to furnish a pyramid for a modern-day p
 haraoh. But for Sofia (Cruz)\, the proposal reeks of the gross inequality 
 that is destroying the world. Bardem and Cruz infuse their roles with comp
 lexity and vulnerability in this tale of affluence\, paranoia\, and ambiti
 on\, where there is nothing more precious than love.... **Purchase Bunker 
 on Tuesday September 15th at 11am. There is one extra ticket (seated toget
 her) available for purchase\; message me if you're interested.**\n\n**COST
 **\nRegular Cost: $35.73 includes all fees\n\nMeetup Organizer Fee: $5\n\n
 **Ticket Policy**: All sales are final\, no refunds or exchanges.\n\n**SIG
 NING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP Yes confirming if you will join for lunch after. (Ev
 eryone goes on the waitlist until they post their seat number or state the
 y will be doing Rush.)**\n* **[Purchase](https://www.ticketmaster.ca/event
 /1000650B16C63801)** **your own ticket for Tuesday\, September 15th at 11a
 m**\, post your seat number and I will move you to going. Note: tickets ar
 e currently showing as sold out\, but that can change at any time as they 
 release more tickets or people make exchanges.\n* Alternately\, you can me
 ssage me for the extra ticket\, and it will be confirmed once payment is r
 eceived by etransfer. Ticket will be provided at the event start time.\n* 
 Rush is also possible\, requiring you to line up 1 hour before showtime. 1
 5 mins prior to start time\, an attendance check is completed and any avai
 lable seats are sold at regular price + $2\n\nA reminder will be sent the 
 day before with my cell and reminder details where to meet and when.\n\nRS
 VPs close 2 days prior. Cancellations will result in a No Show and impact 
 future attendance.\n\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me for the Show at: 10:30am 
 inside the Princess of Wales Theatre at 300 King St. W**\, **on the ground
  floor** **to the right side of the box office after scanning your tickets
 .**\n\n**Start: 11am**\n\nLength: 2 hours 6 mins\n\nAfter: meet at the ini
 tial meeting spot to chat about the show and head out for lunch near by.\n
 \nEnjoy and please post your comments in the Event after.
