SUMMARY:Being Heumann True Story Drama at TIFF 2026 + Dinner (TIFF Lightbo
 x)
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\n**On Saturday September 19th\,** join me t
 o **see Being Heumann at the 51st edition of the Toronto International Fil
 m Festival (TIFF)**. *Heumann* is the opening and closing show for TIFF 20
 26. Featuring a breakout performance by Ruth Madeley and Oscar nominee Mar
 k Ruffalo\, this inspiring historical drama from Oscar-winning filmmaker S
 iân Heder (*CODA*) celebrates the paradigm-shifting activist Judy Heumann
 \, “Mother of the Disability Rights Movement.” Every bit as moving as 
 her Best Picture Oscar winner\, *CODA*\, *Heumann* tells the remarkable tr
 ue story of the woman who led a world-changing campaign for accessibility.
  Judy Heumann rallied a handful\, then dozens\, then hundreds of ordinary 
 Americans with disabilities to push the US government to live up to its co
 mmitments. Though set in the past\, *Being Heumann* couldn’t be more per
 tinent to our present. When change can seem overwhelming\, we need heroes 
 like Judy to galvanize us. **Purchase Being Heumann on Saturday September 
 19th at 6pm. There is one extra ticket (seated together) available for pur
 chase\; message me if you're interested.**\n\n**COST**\nRegular Cost: $35.
 73 includes all fees\n\nMeetup Organizer Fee: $5\n\n**Ticket Policy**: All
  sales are final\, no refunds or exchanges.\n\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP 
 Yes confirming if you will join for dinner after. (Everyone goes on the wa
 itlist until they post their seat number or state they will be doing Rush.
 )**\n* **[Purchase](https://www.ticketmaster.ca/event/1000650B07682680)** 
 **your own ticket for Saturday\, September 19th at 6pm**\, post your seat 
 number and I will move you to going. Note: tickets are currently showing a
 s sold out\, but that can change at any time as they release more tickets 
 or people make exchanges.\n* Alternately\, you can message me for the extr
 a ticket\, and it will be confirmed once payment is received by etransfer.
  Ticket will be provided at the event start time.\n* Rush is also possible
 \, requiring you to line up 1 hour before showtime. 15 mins prior to start
  time\, an attendance check is completed and any available seats are sold 
 at regular price + $2\n\nA reminder will be sent the day before with my ce
 ll and reminder details where to meet and when.\n\nRSVPs close 1 day prior
 . Cancellations will result in a No Show and impact future attendance.\n\n
 **MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me at: 5:30pm inside TIFF Lightbox at 350 King St.
  W**\, **on the ground floor** **to the right side of the box office after
  scanning your tickets.**\n\n**Start: 6pm**\n\nLength: 2 hours 7 mins\n\nA
 fter: meet outside the auditorium to chat about the show and head out for 
 dinner near by.\n\nEnjoy and please post your comments in the Event after.
